            {
                "entry_id": "61fafb4e-3019-3940-842e-5b7c28677d11",
                "word": "amelia",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "7d759571-72ad-4702-9612-0ebbab013ecb",
                        "entry_id": "61fafb4e-3019-3940-842e-5b7c28677d11",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "amelias"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8b6007b2-4e7b-3a9a-bb36-aa39ff2e25be",
                        "entry_id": "61fafb4e-3019-3940-842e-5b7c28677d11",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The congenital absence of one or more limbs."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1e9b232b-6f8f-4079-bd40-a1a1af0d8b88",
                                "sense_id": "8b6007b2-4e7b-3a9a-bb36-aa39ff2e25be",
                                "text": "As already mentioned, limb deficiencies – amelias and meromelias – represent an important group of limb abnormalities."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d949875-9593-4473-a18a-eafa5e92133b",
                                "sense_id": "8b6007b2-4e7b-3a9a-bb36-aa39ff2e25be",
                                "text": "The newborn examination confirms the diagnosis of amelia and distinguishes it from other limb deficiencies (e.g. terminal transverse defects) and sirenomelia."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2b54647d-2d95-4eef-926c-221b6a1c281c",
                                "sense_id": "8b6007b2-4e7b-3a9a-bb36-aa39ff2e25be",
                                "text": "2021, Femi Oyebode, Psychopathology of Rare and Unusual Syndromes, Royal College of Psychiatrists, Cambridge University Press, page 179,\nFurthermore, the fact that people with amelia can experience phantom limbs, despite never having had any limbs, points to the existence of neural systems ready to respond to sensory inputs from limbs."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "65599aca-62e7-432b-b3a4-24598540eb39",
                        "source_entry_id": "61fafb4e-3019-3940-842e-5b7c28677d11",
                        "source_sense_id": "8b6007b2-4e7b-3a9a-bb36-aa39ff2e25be",
                        "source_sense_description": "congenital absence of one or more limbs",
                        "target_lang_word": "amélie",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "amélie",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4b24ad14-287f-3287-b4df-fb5146f04439",
                                        "entry_id": "8cc985fb-0aeb-3ab6-92ec-7961e8a51f35",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Absence congénitale d’un ou de plusieurs membres."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "30b8836e-eed7-4407-872f-4fb1cbcef7a6",
                                                "sense_id": "4b24ad14-287f-3287-b4df-fb5146f04439",
                                                "text": "La thalidomide prescrite contre les nausées des femmes enceintes a provoqué de nombreuses malformations telles que l’amélie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ac1ae04-8100-4618-a0fd-1debb7ca0769",
                                                "sense_id": "4b24ad14-287f-3287-b4df-fb5146f04439",
                                                "text": "D’autres, au contraire, sont compatibles avec la vie comme les phocomélies ou les amélies, récemment mises à l’ordre du jour par les accidents dus à la thalidomide."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
